you mean does it already
have like vinegar,

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:10.520
yeah it's got some sort of
vinegar sauce in the meat.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.610
Okay.
Do you know,

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:16.930
Bojangle's is also now serving
a pulled pork sandwich.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:18.670
It's on the menu, I didn't get that.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:19.600
Really?

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.010
And I'm sorry I have to
throw somebody under the bus,

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.410
just quickly let me do this.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:27.650
Atlantic Beach, on Atlantic Beach,

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:30.420
which is technically an outer bank.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:32.910
Emerald Isle and Atlantic Beach,
they're all on this island.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:34.410
Well there's a Bojangle's on that island

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.490
and I was staying on that
island for a few days.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.890
And I took Shepherd to Bojangle's,

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:41.850
I haven't been to Bojangle's yet.

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:44.553
I get to Bojangle's at Atlantic Beach,

00:11:44.553 --> 00:11:46.504
I get in line and you know how they have,

00:11:46.504 --> 00:11:49.400
the only place in the world that does the,

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.320
Bojangle's is the only place
in the world that does the line

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.210
where you gotta go around
like you're getting ready

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:55.700
to go on a ride.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:56.910
It switches back.

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.470
Oh not in the car, you're
talking about in the restaurant.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.400
In the restaurant there's a switch back

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.550
and then you get up
there and then you order

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:04.130
and they say it into the microphone.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:05.170
It's awesome.

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:07.927
Just wondering why they're
still doing that but--

00:12:07.927 --> 00:12:09.540
That's like an amusement park ride too,

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:10.760
it's like buckle up.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:15.100
The first thing that threw
me off is I'll get in line

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.110
and there's a murmur
going through the line

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.630
and it's that they're out of dirty rice,

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.760
which I wanted dirty rice.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:24.210
I was gonna get dirty rice and beans.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.630
Cajun pintos.
I love the fact

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.665
that made its way back through the line.

00:12:27.665 --> 00:12:29.685
They're out of dirty rice,
what are we gonna do?

00:12:29.685 --> 00:12:30.810
They're out of dirty rice.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.097
The rollercoaster's broke.
Should we leave?

00:12:32.097 --> 00:12:33.583
Should we leave, should we
go back to the mainland?

00:12:33.583 --> 00:12:35.910
Should we go to Morehead City?

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:38.530
Those kinds of things
are happening and then,

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:41.163
I'm like okay well, I don't
have to get dirty rice.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:45.130
45 minutes later--
What?

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.515
Is when I was receiving my food.

00:12:47.515 --> 00:12:51.020
45 minutes later.

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:55.688
This place, I love Bojangle's
but the one in Atlantic Beach

00:12:55.688 --> 00:12:59.240
is so mismanaged that it is a disgrace

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:00.940
to the name of Bojangle's.

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.850
It is, 'cause Locke and his cousins went

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:06.732
and they also had to wait 45
minutes at a different time.

00:13:06.732 --> 00:13:07.860
Different time?
I realize that

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:09.788
it's peak season, but there was--

00:13:09.788 --> 00:13:11.540
You sure you weren't going to Jobangle?

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:13.210
There's 11 people in line.

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.620
There were 11 people in
line and some of them

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:17.440
were like three people
together as a party.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.540
It wasn't 11 different groups,

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.850
it was like four different
groups, 45 minutes.

00:13:21.850 --> 00:13:24.070
Did you band together
with those people and--

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.460
Oh I'm not done.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:27.960
They're out of dirty rice, I get up there,

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:31.277
I order, they're still out
of dirty rice at that point

00:13:31.277 --> 00:13:33.003
and I didn't even ask for it.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.571
They're out of honey mustard.

00:13:35.571 --> 00:13:36.404
Gah.

00:13:37.406 --> 00:13:38.480
Hey man post-apocalyptic.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:41.793
Then we get our tea, of
course we got sweet tea.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.640
Jessie wanted, she said bring
me back an unsweetened tea

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.390
and then Shepherd and I were
like we're gonna get sweet tea

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:49.060
because we're here.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:49.893
When in Rome.

00:13:49.893 --> 00:13:52.100
We sit down and Shepherd's
like I think I got Mom's tea

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.170
and he says let me taste, and
he taste another, says no,

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:56.010
and then he tastes mine, says
Dad these are all unsweetened.

00:13:56.010 --> 00:13:58.960
I was like Shepherd, this is
just your 10 year old palate.

00:13:58.960 --> 00:13:59.960
Let me taste them.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.110
They're all unsweet.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:05.040
I go back up and I say
sorry, you put unsweet tea

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.890
in these sweet teas, he's like okay.

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:08.291
45 minutes later.

00:14:08.291 --> 00:14:09.980
That happened in about seven minutes,

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.650
it wasn't too long.
Okay.

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:13.190
He fills 'em back up, we go back down

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:15.300
and Shepherd says Dad
they're still unsweet.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:17.020
I taste 'em, he's right.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:19.343
They have not put any
sugar in the sweet tea.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:24.130
I begin to see people who've
already waited 45 minutes

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:26.870
for their meal getting up
and looking at their tea.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:28.750
There's an old man walking
by, he's talking to himself.

00:14:28.750 --> 00:14:30.428
I was like, the tea's not sweet is it?

00:14:30.428 --> 00:14:32.720
He didn't even hear me, he was like .

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.630
He goes up, he gets his tea,
and then there's a woman

00:14:35.630 --> 00:14:37.930
back there, she's like,
y'all, the tea's not sweet.

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:38.770
This is bad.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:40.673
I mean this is like--

00:14:40.673 --> 00:14:42.223
They forgot to put sugar in the tea.

00:14:42.223 --> 00:14:44.850
This is the start of a
riot in North Carolina.

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:47.493
If there's a Bojangle's
representative listening,

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:51.800
send help to the one
in Atlantic Beach, man,

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:54.196
because I'm not gonna go to it anymore.

00:14:54.196 --> 00:14:57.810
I don't wanna ruin, the food is so good.

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:59.472
I mean when Bojangle's
runs out of dirty rice--

00:14:59.472 --> 00:15:00.305
But I don't wanna wait an hour for it.

00:15:00.305 --> 00:15:03.570
Honey mustard, you need
to air drop some supplies.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:06.650
And I believe in--
Air drop a manager in there.

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:10.200
I believe that it might
be actual sacrilege

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.510
to serve sweet tea that's not sweet.

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.370
I think those people might go to hell.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:15.203
Me too.

00:15:15.203 --> 00:15:17.560
I think that might be an unforgivable sin.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.973
Right, especially when they're
like no, but this one is.

00:15:20.973 --> 00:15:22.890
And if you do it twice, yes, yes,

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:26.723
you go to the third level of hell.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:30.400
Sorry for that little rant,
I didn't expect to do that,

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:34.620
but I was really upset, very upset.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.100
I would be afraid.

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:38.460
With those things
happening at a Bojangle's,

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:42.470
I would literally, I would be
like, kids, we gotta get out

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:44.880
of here 'cause something
bad's gonna happen.

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:47.766
Like, someone is gonna get too upset

00:15:47.766 --> 00:15:49.700
and there's gonna be like,

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:52.230
they're gonna be rippin' paper bags

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:55.370
and I don't know, throwing tenders.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:56.792
Yeah.

00:15:56.792 --> 00:15:57.625
Well they don't call 'em tenders--

00:15:57.625 --> 00:15:58.930
They call 'em supremes.
Supremes.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.890
They also have homestyle tenders.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:01.723
Yeah they're not hot.

00:16:01.723 --> 00:16:03.044
They don't have the spice in them.

00:16:03.044 --> 00:16:03.877
They're for the children.

00:16:03.877 --> 00:16:06.270
Yeah I saw a full-grown man order those.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:07.200
For the weak.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.650
I shook my head at that guy.
For the weak men

00:16:09.650 --> 00:16:10.970
and children.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:14.250
'Cause it's not that hot.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.620
Oh man so you're hurtin'.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:18.260
I feel good now that
I got that out though.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:20.510
You got that Cook Out in you.

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:23.690
I got this, man, it was like,

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:27.960
it was beets and yams and
they have this thing--

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:28.910
Yum.
They had a thing

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:31.400
