your lips can be drinking from our mugs.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.144
Mythical.store.

00:18:00.144 --> 00:18:01.970
Thical.store.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:05.568
We will--
Did a little--

00:18:05.568 --> 00:18:06.401
It could have been quesadilla.

00:18:06.401 --> 00:18:08.217
Enchilada come up?
It could have been breading.

00:18:08.217 --> 00:18:09.460
It could have been the
little hard breading

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:11.050
on the stick at the bottom of a corn dog.

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:12.090
That sticks with you awhile, you know,

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.200
and I always eat the--

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.400
Oh you nibble that stuff off.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.415
Oh that's the best part.

00:18:15.415 --> 00:18:16.720
You nibble nibble nibble.
Listen.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:19.690
You nibble that stick.
I would buy sticks

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.440
of just the hard, crusty batter.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:23.860
You know what you can do is you can go

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:24.980
through the trash can of a Cook Out.

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:26.140
Crusty sticks.
You can go through

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:27.527
the Cook Out trash can.
Crusty sticks.

00:18:27.527 --> 00:18:30.080
And get out the corn dog sticks.

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.350
No but people eat 'em in
